        "text": "while vs do-while loops in Java",
        "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004", "Q0005"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "A while loop checks its condition before executing the loop body, so if the condition is false the body never runs. A do-while loop checks the condition after executing the body, guaranteeing that the body runs at least once even when the condition is false.",
        "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004", "Q0005"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    }
  ],
